### Health check

GET http://localhost:3000/health

### Create valid order

POST http://localhost:3000/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "externalId": "ORDER-1002",
  "customerName": "Example Company",
  "customerEmail": "orders@example.com",
  "amount": 999.99,
  "currency": "PLN"
}

### Create invalid order

POST http://localhost:3000/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "externalId": "",
  "customerName": "",
  "customerEmail": "to-nie-jest-email",
  "amount": -500,
  "currency": "ZIEMNIAK"
}

### Get all orders

GET http://localhost:3000/api/orders

### Get order by ID

GET http://localhost:3000/api/orders/1

### Get nonexistent order

GET http://localhost:3000/api/orders/999999

### Get order with invalid ID

GET http://localhost:3000/api/orders/abc

### Order status workflow
# Set this to an existing order ID in RECEIVED status before running the workflow

@statusOrderId = 4

### Update order status: RECEIVED -> PROCESSING

PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/orders/{{statusOrderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PROCESSING"
}

### Update order status: PROCESSING -> COMPLETED

PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/orders/{{statusOrderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "COMPLETED"
}

### Invalid transition: COMPLETED -> PROCESSING

PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/orders/{{statusOrderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PROCESSING"
}

### Invalid status

PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/orders/{{statusOrderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "ZIEMNIAK"
}

### Update nonexistent order

PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/orders/999999/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PROCESSING"
}
